 # Continuous LOD (CLOD)
 
-Also called: Continuous Levels of Detail (LOD) Nodes, LOD Nodes, Levels of Detail, Smooth LOD Blending
+Also called: Continuous Level of Detail
 
 ## Overview
-Continuous LOD (CLOD) is a technique that replaces a high-resolution implicit function with a more efficient low-resolution expression by interpolating between them based on the viewer's position, ensuring the region of influence depends on the viewer rather than the object center [S1]. Unlike traditional LOD which selects a single model based on distance to the object center, CLOD adapts the implicit surface continuously based on the distance between the viewer and the query point, straddling or embedding the surface [S1]. It sets itself apart from proxy nodes by allowing the transition region to intersect the surface and from discrete LOD methods by eliminating sudden visual changes through smooth blending [S1].
+Continuous LOD (CLOD) is a multiresolution technique that replaces a high-resolution implicit function or point cloud with a more efficient low-resolution representation by interpolating between them based on the viewer's position [S2]. Unlike traditional distance-based LOD which selects a single model based on distance to the object center, CLOD adapts the representation continuously based on the distance between the viewer and the query point, allowing the transition region to straddle or embed the surface [S2]. It sets itself apart from proxy nodes by making the region of influence dependent on the viewer position, and from discrete LOD methods by eliminating sudden visual changes through smooth blending [S2]. The technique builds upon [Progressive Level Transitions](14190-progressive-level-transitions.md) and operates alongside [Piecewise Linear LOD Transition](22725-piecewise-linear-lod-transition.md).
 
