+5.  **Point Cloud Filtering (Alternative):** For point clouds, assign each point an LOD value (0–3) based on spatial density. LOD 0 covers 1×1×1 m volumes, LOD 1 covers 0.5×0.5×0.5 m, and LOD 2 covers 0.25×0.25×0.25 m. Average the color of all points within each volume to prevent aliasing [S1, unofficial]. At runtime, iterate over points, perform frustum culling, compare distance to assigned LOD level, and apply a randomized normalized weight for smooth blending before copying visible points to a render buffer [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Parameters:**
-*   $r$: The radius defining the start of the transition zone from the viewer. Inside this radius, the high-resolution model is used ($\alpha=0$) [S1].
-*   $\delta_r$: The width of the transition zone. Interpolation occurs in the range $r \le d(p, e) \le r + \delta_r$ [S1].
